---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A web app with 400 transitive dependencies. A popular package ships a malicious patch on day 10. Pick how you take updates and see who gets hurt.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Floating ranges</b> and leave detection at <b>5 days</b>: every build resolves the newest version, so <b>every build from day 10 to day 14</b> pulls the malicious release. A <b>lockfile updated every 7 days</b> only pulls it if the bot happens to run inside that window (it does, on day 14), and then keeps it through day 16, so <b>22 builds</b> instead of 44.</li>
    <li>Raise <b>Minimum release age</b> to <b>6 days</b> with the lockfile: nothing younger than 6 days is adopted, so the malicious release is yanked (day 15) before it is eligible (day 16) and <b>0 builds</b> take it. Now read the <b>Known CVE fix</b> box: the real fix, published on day 12, is adopted <b>9 days late</b> (6 for the age gate, then the wait for the next weekly bot run). Floating with the same age gate is 6 days late.</li>
    <li>Switch the attack to <b>Existing version re-uploaded with new bytes</b>. A release-age gate does nothing here, because no new version appeared. With the lockfile and <b>Verify SHA-256 integrity</b> on, builds fail closed instead of installing the bad bytes. Floating builds have no recorded hash and are hit.</li>
    <li>Pick <b>Pinned exact + manual review</b>: with detection at 5 days no review lands in the window (reviews are on day 21 and 42), so <b>0 builds</b> are hit, but the CVE fix is <b>9 days late</b>. Push detection to <b>14 days</b> and the day 21 review adopts the bad release: <b>37 builds</b>, unless you tick <b>Reviewer reads the diff</b>.</li>
    <li>In <b>Dependency confusion</b> compare the two lines: an unscoped internal name loses to a higher public version on the first build (floating) or the next lockfile update; a <b>scoped registry rule</b> never asks the public registry at all.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg scs" data-scs>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Version policy
        <select class="pg-in" data-policy>
          <option value="floating">Floating ranges (^1.2.0, no lockfile)</option>
          <option value="lockfile" selected>Lockfile, bot updates every N days</option>
          <option value="pinned">Pinned exact + manual review (every 21 days)</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Attack
        <select class="pg-in" data-kind>
          <option value="release" selected>New malicious patch release</option>
          <option value="tamper">Existing version re-uploaded with new bytes</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Lockfile update every <input type="range" min="1" max="30" value="7" data-every /> <b data-everyval>7</b> days</label>
      <label>Minimum release age <input type="range" min="0" max="14" value="0" data-age /> <b data-ageval>0</b> days</label>
      <label>Detected and yanked after <input type="range" min="1" max="14" value="5" data-detect /> <b data-detectval>5</b> days</label>
      <label>Seed <input type="number" class="pg-in scs-seed" min="1" max="99" value="7" data-seed /></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="scs-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-integrity /> Verify SHA-256 integrity</label>
      <label class="scs-check"><input type="checkbox" data-scoped /> Scoped registry rule for internal names</label>
      <label class="scs-check"><input type="checkbox" data-noscripts /> Ignore install scripts</label>
      <label class="scs-check"><input type="checkbox" data-reviewer /> Reviewer reads the diff of each bump</label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="scs-strip" role="img" data-strip aria-label="Timeline of builds"></div>
    <div class="scs-events" aria-hidden="true" data-events></div>
    <p class="pg-note scs-legend"><i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--role-2)"></i> clean build <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--bad)"></i> pulled the bad version <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--role-3)"></i> failed closed on a hash mismatch. Below: <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--muted)"></i> dependency resolution runs, <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--bad)"></i> day 10 malicious publish, <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--accent)"></i> yank, <i class="scs-sw" style="--c: var(--role-3)"></i> day 12 real CVE fix published. Days 0 to 59, bar height is builds that day.</p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-box="bad"><h3>Malicious release</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-bad></span><span class="pg-note" data-badnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-box="cve"><h3>Known CVE fix</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-cve></span><span class="pg-note" data-cvenote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-box="conf"><h3>Dependency confusion</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-conf1></span><span class="pg-mono" data-conf2></span><span class="pg-note" data-confnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-box="blast" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Blast radius</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-blast></span><span class="pg-note" data-ci></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: 4 to 12 builds a day (seeded); malicious payload sits in an install script and also ships in the bundle; the real CVE fix is a separate in-range release on day 12; lockfile and pinned installs keep a bad version until the next update or until a manual fix 2 days after the yank; the minimum release age applies to every resolution except where noted; cached tarballs and CI caches are ignored.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../playground';
  // ---core--- pure functions, no DOM
  interface Cfg { policy: 'floating' | 'lockfile' | 'pinned'; kind: 'release' | 'tamper'; every: number; minAge: number; detect: number; integrity: boolean; scoped: boolean; noScripts: boolean; reviewer: boolean; seed: number }
  interface Tree { total: number; direct: number; target: number; dependents: number; viaDirect: number; depth: number }
  const H = 60; const ATTACK = 10; const CVE = 12; const REVIEW = 21; const RESPONSE = 2; const N = 400; const DIRECT = 12;
  const DIRECT_FANOUT = 3; // each direct dependency pulls in 3 packages
  const P_TWO_DEPS = 0.55; // otherwise a package has 2 deps with this chance, else 1 or 3 evenly
  const ATTACH_WEIGHT = 3; // preferential attachment: weight per existing dependent
  const TARGET_SHARE_DIV = 4; // the attacked package is used by about a quarter of the tree
  const BUILDS = { min: 4, span: 9 }; // builds per day, 4..12
  const MAX_SEED = 99; const CVE_LATE_DAYS = 7; // CVE fix later than this is marked bad

  function mulberry32(a: number) {
    return () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };
  }

  function makeTree(seed: number): Tree {
    const rnd = mulberry32(seed * 7919 + 13); // spread the small seeds apart
    const deps: number[][] = Array.from({ length: N }, () => []);
    const indeg = new Array(N).fill(0);
    for (let i = 0; i < N - 1; i++) {
      const k = i < DIRECT ? DIRECT_FANOUT : rnd() < P_TWO_DEPS ? 2 : rnd() < 0.5 ? 1 : 3;
      for (let t = 0; t < k; t++) {
        // preferential attachment: popular libraries (already depended on) attract more dependents
        let w = 0; for (let j = i + 1; j < N; j++) w += 1 + ATTACH_WEIGHT * indeg[j];
        let r = rnd() * w; let pick = N - 1;
        for (let j = i + 1; j < N; j++) { r -= 1 + ATTACH_WEIGHT * indeg[j]; if (r <= 0) { pick = j; break; } }
        if (!deps[i].includes(pick)) { deps[i].push(pick); indeg[pick]++; }
      }
    }
    for (let k = DIRECT; k < N; k++) if (indeg[k] === 0) { const p = Math.floor(rnd() * k); deps[p].push(k); indeg[k]++; }
    const parents: number[][] = Array.from({ length: N }, () => []);
    deps.forEach((ds, i) => ds.forEach((d) => parents[d].push(i)));
    let target = DIRECT; let best = -1; let bestSet: Set<number> = new Set();
    for (let t = DIRECT; t < N; t++) {
      const seen = new Set<number>(); const stack = [...parents[t]];
      while (stack.length) { const x = stack.pop()!; if (seen.has(x)) continue; seen.add(x); stack.push(...parents[x]); }
      // "a popular package": the one used by about a quarter of the tree (a library used by everything is rarer than the headlines suggest)
      if (best < 0 || Math.abs(seen.size - N / TARGET_SHARE_DIV) < Math.abs(best - N / TARGET_SHARE_DIV)) { best = seen.size; target = t; bestSet = seen; }
    }
    const dist = new Array(N).fill(-1); let frontier: number[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < DIRECT; i++) { dist[i] = 1; frontier.push(i); }
    while (frontier.length) { const nx: number[] = []; for (const x of frontier) for (const d of deps[x]) if (dist[d] < 0) { dist[d] = dist[x] + 1; nx.push(d); } frontier = nx; }
    let viaDirect = 0; bestSet.forEach((x) => { if (x < DIRECT) viaDirect++; });
    return { total: N, direct: DIRECT, target, dependents: bestSet.size, viaDirect, depth: dist[target] };
  }

  function buildsPerDay(seed: number): number[] {
    const rnd = mulberry32(seed * 104729 + 7); // a second stream, independent of the tree
    return Array.from({ length: H }, () => BUILDS.min + Math.floor(rnd() * BUILDS.span));
  }

  // The days on which the dependency set is re-resolved for this policy.
  function isResolveDay(c: Cfg, day: number): boolean {
    if (c.policy === 'floating') return true;
    if (day <= 0) return false;
    return c.policy === 'lockfile' ? day % c.every === 0 : day % REVIEW === 0;
  }

  function simulate(c: Cfg) {
    const builds = buildsPerDay(c.seed);
    const yank = ATTACK + c.detect;
    const bad: number[] = new Array(H).fill(0); const failed: number[] = new Array(H).fill(0);
    let lockedBad = false;
    for (let d = 0; d < H; d++) {
      const live = d >= ATTACK && d < yank;
      if (c.kind === 'release') {
        if (isResolveDay(c, d)) {
          let cand = live && d >= ATTACK + c.minAge;
          if (c.policy === 'pinned' && c.reviewer) cand = false;
          lockedBad = cand;
        }
        if (c.policy !== 'floating' && d >= yank + RESPONSE) lockedBad = false;
        if (lockedBad) bad[d] = builds[d];
      } else if (live) {
        // same version string, different bytes: only a recorded hash can notice
        if (c.policy !== 'floating' && c.integrity) failed[d] = builds[d]; else bad[d] = builds[d];
      }
    }
    const sum = (a: number[]) => a.reduce((x, y) => x + y, 0);
    const days = bad.map((b, i) => (b > 0 ? i : -1)).filter((i) => i >= 0);
    const totalBuilds = sum(builds); const badBuilds = sum(bad); const failedBuilds = sum(failed);
    let adopted = -1;
    for (let d = CVE + c.minAge; d < H; d++) if (isResolveDay(c, d)) { adopted = d; break; }
    let vulnBuilds = 0; for (let d = CVE; d < (adopted < 0 ? H : adopted); d++) vulnBuilds += builds[d];
    return {
      builds, bad, failed, totalBuilds, badBuilds, failedBuilds,
      firstBad: days.length ? days[0] : -1, lastBad: days.length ? days[days.length - 1] : -1, windowDays: days.length ? days[days.length - 1] - days[0] + 1 : 0,
      ciRuns: c.noScripts ? 0 : badBuilds,
      cve: { adopted, delay: adopted < 0 ? -1 : adopted - CVE, vulnBuilds },
      confusion: { unscoped: confusion(c, false), scoped: confusion(c, true) },
      yank,
    };
  }

  // Internal package acme-billing 1.4.2; the attacker publishes the same name publicly with a higher version on day 10.
  function confusion(c: Cfg, scoped: boolean): { hit: boolean; day: number } {
    if (scoped) return { hit: false, day: -1 };
    if (c.policy === 'pinned' && c.reviewer) return { hit: false, day: -1 };
    for (let d = ATTACK + c.minAge; d < ATTACK + c.detect; d++) if (isResolveDay(c, d)) return { hit: true, day: d };
    return { hit: false, day: -1 };
  }
  // ---end core---

  const treeCache = new Map<number, Tree>();
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-scs]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const num = numberValue(q);
    const chk = (s: string) => q<HTMLInputElement>(s).checked;
    const strip = q('[data-strip]'); const events = q('[data-events]');
    const cells: HTMLElement[] = []; const evs: HTMLElement[] = [];
    for (let d = 0; d < H; d++) {
      const c = document.createElement('i'); c.className = 'scs-cell'; const b = document.createElement('i'); b.style.height = '0%'; c.appendChild(b); strip.appendChild(c); cells.push(c);
      const e = document.createElement('i'); e.className = 'scs-ev'; events.appendChild(e); evs.push(e);
    }
    let queued = false;

    function read(): Cfg {
      const seed = Math.min(MAX_SEED, Math.max(1, Math.floor(num('[data-seed]')) || 1));
      return { policy: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value as Cfg['policy'], kind: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-kind]').value as Cfg['kind'], every: num('[data-every]'), minAge: num('[data-age]'), detect: num('[data-detect]'), integrity: chk('[data-integrity]'), scoped: chk('[data-scoped]'), noScripts: chk('[data-noscripts]'), reviewer: chk('[data-reviewer]'), seed };
    }
    const plural = (n: number, w: string) => `${n} ${w}${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;

    function draw() {
      queued = false;
      const c = read(); const r = simulate(c);
      if (!treeCache.has(c.seed)) treeCache.set(c.seed, makeTree(c.seed));
      const t = treeCache.get(c.seed)!;
      q('[data-everyval]').textContent = String(c.every); q('[data-ageval]').textContent = String(c.minAge); q('[data-detectval]').textContent = String(c.detect);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-every]').disabled = c.policy !== 'lockfile';
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-reviewer]').disabled = c.policy !== 'pinned';
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-integrity]').disabled = c.policy === 'floating';
      const maxB = Math.max(...r.builds);
      for (let d = 0; d < H; d++) {
        const cell = cells[d]; const bar = cell.firstElementChild as HTMLElement;
        bar.style.height = `${Math.round((r.builds[d] / maxB) * 100)}%`;
        bar.style.setProperty('--c', r.bad[d] > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : r.failed[d] > 0 ? 'var(--role-3)' : 'var(--role-2)');
        cell.title = `day ${d}: ${r.builds[d]} builds${r.bad[d] ? ', bad version' : r.failed[d] ? ', failed closed' : ''}`;
        const ev = evs[d]; const resolve = isResolveDay(c, d);
        const colour = d === ATTACK ? 'var(--bad)' : d === r.yank ? 'var(--accent)' : d === CVE ? 'var(--role-3)' : resolve ? 'var(--muted)' : 'transparent';
        ev.style.setProperty('--c', colour);
        ev.title = `day ${d}${d === ATTACK ? ': malicious publish' : d === r.yank ? ': yanked' : d === CVE ? ': CVE fix published' : ''}${resolve ? ' (dependencies re-resolved)' : ''}`;
      }
      strip.setAttribute('aria-label', `Builds per day for ${H} days: ${r.badBuilds} of ${r.totalBuilds} pulled the bad version, ${r.failedBuilds} failed closed.`);

      q('[data-bad]').textContent = c.kind === 'release' || r.failedBuilds === 0 ? `${r.badBuilds} of ${r.totalBuilds} builds` : `${r.badBuilds} bad, ${r.failedBuilds} failed closed`;
      q('[data-badnote]').textContent = r.badBuilds > 0
        ? `first on day ${r.firstBad}, last on day ${r.lastBad}: exposed for ${plural(r.windowDays, 'day')}. Yanked on day ${r.yank}${c.policy !== 'floating' && c.kind === 'release' ? `, and your lock kept it until day ${r.lastBad + 1}` : ''}. Payload ran on ${r.ciRuns} CI runners (install script${c.noScripts ? 's ignored' : ''}) and shipped in ${r.badBuilds} builds.`
        : r.failedBuilds > 0 ? `every download of the swapped file failed the recorded hash, so ${r.failedBuilds} builds stopped instead of shipping it. Loud, but nothing bad ran.` : 'no build resolved the bad version before it was yanked.';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-box=bad]').style.setProperty('--c', r.badBuilds > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-2)');

      q('[data-cve]').textContent = r.cve.adopted < 0 ? `not adopted within ${H} days` : `adopted on day ${r.cve.adopted}: ${plural(r.cve.delay, 'day')} late`;
      q('[data-cvenote]').textContent = `fix published day ${CVE}; ${r.cve.vulnBuilds} builds shipped the vulnerable version in the meantime.`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-box=cve]').style.setProperty('--c', r.cve.delay > CVE_LATE_DAYS || r.cve.delay < 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : r.cve.delay > 0 ? 'var(--role-3)' : 'var(--role-2)');

      const u = r.confusion.unscoped; const s = r.confusion.scoped;
      q('[data-conf1]').textContent = u.hit ? `Unscoped: SUCCEEDS on day ${u.day}` : 'Unscoped: blocked';
      q('[data-conf2]').textContent = `Scoped rule: ${s.hit ? 'SUCCEEDS' : 'blocked'}`;
      q('[data-confnote]').textContent = (c.scoped ? 'Your setting has the scoped rule on. ' : 'Your setting has the scoped rule off. ') + (u.hit ? 'The public acme-billing 99.0.0 is higher than the internal 1.4.2, so the resolver takes it. ' : c.policy === 'pinned' && c.reviewer ? 'The reviewer rejects the surprise registry. ' : 'No re-resolution happened while the fake was listed. ') + 'Scoping removes the choice: @acme/* only resolves from the private registry.';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-box=conf]').style.setProperty('--c', (c.scoped ? s.hit : u.hit) ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-2)');

      q('[data-blast]').textContent = `popular-lib: used by ${t.dependents} of ${t.total} packages, via ${t.viaDirect} of ${t.direct} direct dependencies`;
      q('[data-ci]').textContent = `Sits ${t.depth} level${t.depth === 1 ? '' : 's'} deep from your app. You never chose it directly, but you run its code.`;

      const bits: string[] = [];
      bits.push(r.badBuilds > 0 ? `${r.badBuilds} builds took the bad code` : r.failedBuilds > 0 ? `0 builds took the bad code (${r.failedBuilds} failed closed)` : 'the malicious release never reached a build');
      bits.push(r.cve.adopted < 0 ? `the real CVE fix was not adopted in ${H} days` : r.cve.delay === 0 ? 'the real CVE fix landed the day it was published' : `the real CVE fix landed ${plural(r.cve.delay, 'day')} late`);
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = `This policy: ${bits.join('; ')}.`;
      q('[data-verdict]').classList.toggle('bad', r.badBuilds > 0);
    }
    function schedule() { if (!queued) { queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(draw); } }
    const defaults = { policy: 'lockfile', kind: 'release', every: '7', age: '0', detect: '5', seed: '7' };
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value = defaults.policy; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-kind]').value = defaults.kind;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-every]').value = defaults.every; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-age]').value = defaults.age; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-detect]').value = defaults.detect; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value = defaults.seed;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-integrity]').checked = true; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-scoped]').checked = false; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-noscripts]').checked = false; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-reviewer]').checked = false;
      draw();
    });
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .scs-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .scs-seed { width: 5rem; }
  .playground .scs-strip { display: flex; gap: 1px; align-items: flex-end; height: 64px; }
  .playground .scs-cell { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; height: 100%; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; }
  .playground .scs-cell > i { display: block; width: 100%; background: var(--c, var(--role-2)); border-radius: 1px 1px 0 0; }
  .playground .scs-events { display: flex; gap: 1px; height: 8px; }
  .playground .scs-ev { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; background: var(--c, transparent); }
  .playground .scs-sw { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--c); vertical-align: -1px; }
  .playground .scs-legend { line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
